        "id": "ch1_6_3-2",
        "text": "ESTABLISHED\nIt\u2019s essential to understand what each option means:\nI\nI -a/--all : Display all the sockets. Take note that this option is very ver-\nbose; thus, we need to combine it with the following options (to filter the\noutput).\nI\nI -n/--numeric : Do not resolve names. In the previous command, you saw\nthat the IP address is followed by the port number. If I don\u2019t use the -n\noption, then the tool will try to figure out the service name (for example,\nfor 80, it\u2019s going to be HTTP instead).\nChapter 1 I Mastering the Terminal Window\n47\nI\nI -t/--tcp : Display TCP connections.\nI\nI -u/--udp : Display UDP connections.",
